nodes.title:
Proposed: treat ElevenLabs Agents as the strongest global rival for Indian enterprise voice. It is not just a TTS vendor: it has India residency, native Exotel, Indian GTM hires and Indian agent logos, and a campaign product in the pipeline. Score VP against it on five runnable tasks:
- handset reply gap on Indian PSTN on a standard (non-Enterprise) plan;
- Hinglish language hold on the default configuration;
- recurring 09:00-21:00 IST windows with per-lead retries and suppression;
- messy-CSV hygiene (+91 normalisation, dedupe, opt-out);
- Indian carrier and regulatory failure reasons in plain language.

events.details:
ElevenLabs Agents lane (account-free) finished. Work done:
- read the 804-page llms.txt (258 pages saved), the OpenAPI (322 paths), pricing, 32 changelog entries and the status RSS;
- unpacked 6 npm SDKs and the PyPI wheel;
- resolved 19 hostnames (DoH) and matched them to GCP ranges and RDAP;
- captured elevenlabs.io/agents and the signed-out app, and made one 25 s public demo call (WebSocket, react_sdk 0.14.0-beta.0);
- read 157 job posts, Trustpilot, GitHub issues and HN via WebFetch/Algolia.
Outputs: claims.json (56), predictions.json (EL-P01..P12), pricing-allin.json (INR 8.17-8.92/min via Exotel/Plivo), bundle-endpoints.json (326 unpublished convai routes, incl. outbound-campaigns and memories), velocity.json and manifest.csv (3,809 files).
REA: inspect-web-network-capture needed percent-encoded URLs, then gave no stack inference; analyze-javascript-application ran in 6 s but left host literals unresolved.
Blocked and not bypassed: Reddit, G2, the GitHub API and curl HTML (403).
